--TEST--
`Core\Router\Match::attribute<T>()` with a `T` that is not an attribute declaration does not compile: `E1008` — `rule:routing/a-match-reads-an-attribute-as-data` and `rule:attributes/a-retrieval-matches-the-declaration-it-names`
--FILE--
<?nvs
attribute Limit on method { limit: int }

class Shop {
    #[Core\Route(path: "/shop", method: Core\Http\Method::Get)]
    #[Core\Access(allow: Core\Audience::Public)]
    #[Limit(limit: 10)]
    public function index(): void {}
}

?Core\Router\Match $shop = Core\Router::match(Core\Http\Method::Get, "/shop");
?int $limit = $shop?->attribute<int>();
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E1008]: a retrieval's type argument must name an attribute declaration, and `int` is not an attribute declaration
   --> case.nvs:12:33
   |
12 | ?int $limit = $shop?->attribute<int>();
   |                                 ^^^ not an attribute declaration
   = help: declare the attribute with `attribute Name on … { … }`, and write its name here. The call then returns the attributes written with that name

error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
